<title>BELGIUM: Fimeuse H1 1996 profit plunges.</title>
<headline>Fimeuse H1 1996 profit plunges.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996 (in millions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		     5  vs  58</p>
<p>    Cons current profit		 5  vs  58</p>
<p>    Cons extraordinary gain/loss    0  vs   0</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian holding company Fimeuse said the sharp fall in its profit was due to expansion at engineering company  Group Fabricom SA, its main asset.</p>
<p>In a statement, Fimeuse reiterated that its controlling shareholder, Belgian holding company Tractebel SA, planned to absorb the company at an extraordinary shareholders meeting in December.</p>
<p>Tractebel owns more than 96 percent of Fimeuse following a financial restructuring of the company in April.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
